A||N||20||Fiero5||Busted in the Formula!!||||9||
Z||000000||Fiero5||05-09-2001||08:36 AM||||Well, I took Marians Formula up for inspection yesterday afternoon. It was already past the 10 day grace period. Everything went fine, except for one of the stupid front parking light sockets was bad and the light wouldn't stay on consistantly. It was near closing and he didn't have the correct socket anyway, so I said I would take it back home and my Dad and I could do it. We would then bring it back up another day for them to check it and put on the sticker.<BR>I am just coming up on my last turn to my road, and I have to waite for a couple of cars to go by. The second one is, you guessed it, a NH state trooper. As soon as they go by I drive onto my road, but I notice that they have quickly flipped on the blue lights and are doing a fast U turn. I don't make it more than a few hundred feet as they probably thought I dove onto that street to try and avoid them. They flip the siren on a few times to let me know that I need to stop NOW. I wanted to make it to my driveway &gt;sigh&lt;<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Busted_in_the_Formula.JPG"> <BR>I had the digital camera with me from school, so I took a quick pic.<BR>I tell them once they come up to the Formula (there were two of them in the cruiser and they walked up to the Fiero from both sides) the whole story about the socket and fixing it and getting the sticker the next day or so, yada, yada.<BR>They said OK and went back to the cruiser to check my license and the reg for the Formula. After what seemed like an hour, the driver of the cruiser finally came back and said that I was "fine as long as this Fiero has a sticker on it the next time it is heading home."<BR>He then said, "Hey, by the way. Happy Birthday." At first I thought he was being sarcastic or something. Then I remembered, my Birthday was May 7th, the day before. That was pretty cool! <BR>#whew#||||reg||9
Z||000001||84Bill||05-09-2001||08:41 AM||||LOL!! thats an awsome picture!! pretty cool story too.<BR>BTW Happy Birthday!<p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-09-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||JSocha||05-09-2001||09:17 AM||||Happy Belated Birthday!<P>Good thing you weren't good friends with the officer, otherwise he could have given you his Birthday Gift, a ticket!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||05-09-2001||09:27 AM||||Man, I wish I had your luck.  On Monday, I went out for lunch, and when I got to the school parking lot, there was mud all over my frickin car.  Some stupid ass in his 2WD S-10 was doin a big frickin sidesteer and threw mud all over the lane of cars.  I couldn't leave it, so I took it to the car wash.  I then went for a drive to let it dry off.  I only have a 25 minute lunch, so I was in a little hurry.  I was a few miles from the school, and I was going a little fast, I guess.  I wasn't paying attention, and there was a cop cresting the hill.  By the time my passenger told me of him, he already had me.  My radar detector didn't work because of the hill.  So I pull over right away, making it easier for him so he might reduce the ticket.  Seems I was going 64 in a 40, but I wouldn't know because I didn't look at my speedo.  I was very nice to him, again so I could get a reduced ticket, but nope.  I got one for 24 over; $97; half my pay check.  I also got to school nine minutes late.  Then I had to tear off the tinted plastic plate covers too.  Now my parents won't let me do anything performance wise to my GT.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I know it was my fault though.  I guess it pays to slow down.<P>---Happy birthday man!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-09-2001||09:31 AM||||Geeze Steve! whenever a cop stops you keep both hands on the top of the steering wheel, dont reach over to get anything from anywhere, and dont move till the cop tell you to do something.<P>  Esp dont be pointing anything at the cops: camera, camcorder, binoculars, telescope, squirtgun, finger, tongue, torque wrench, faulty parking light socket...<P>  I'll bet you one or both of those troopers had the safety off and had their hand on their pistol grip as they approached your car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero5||05-09-2001||09:59 AM||||Hmm, "Look Jim, he's pulling something out of the passengers side. Quick, pull out 'ole bessy". Guess I didn't think about that! <BR>Yeah, I remember they "both" had one hand on their belt/gun section. It was pretty creepy at first watching them come up like that on both sides of the Fiero. I kept looking at one side mirror and then the other watching them as they slowly walked up.<BR>But as usuall, everything worked out fine in the end.||||reg||11
Z||000006||fierohoho||05-09-2001||10:34 AM||||Fiero5, I know for a fact there are cops out there who like Fieros, I have 3 myself. Glad you ran into another one.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||05-09-2001||10:38 AM||||"But as usuall, everything worked out fine in the end."<P>you only get to post this when everything works out fine.<P>when something goes terribly wrong then we will be wondering, "what ever happend to Steve?"<P>BTW that is a great camera, what kind is it? I been thinking of getting one for $100 or so to keep in the glove 'compartment'. Everytime I see something awesome or incredible, I never have a camera handy.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fiero5||05-09-2001||10:59 AM||||The Digital camera is an Olympus D-460 Zoom 1.3 Megapixel. Just aim and shoot.<BR>It takes great pics as you have seen lately on my posts.<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000009||mrgone||05-09-2001||11:43 AM||||the police station is really close to my apartment building, they tail me ALL the time. im always scared, ive only got about 60kms of 5 speed experience as this is my first manny tranny car.<P>cops scare me||||reg||1
Z||000010||JSocha||05-09-2001||11:55 AM||||fropuff, don't know what kind of RD you have, but after you pay your ticket, get a little cash in the back pocket, you might consider visiting this site and updating yours.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.valentine1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.valentine1.com</A> <P>Mine can pick up Radar and Laser (I swear) up to 5 miles away in any direction and still pick up a signals when approaching hills.  <P>Rugby got a new laser gun and they were trying it out at the cop shop back in Feb and my Valentine detector was going nuts the whole day and I thought it was broke.  It just happened it was picking some stray signals up (don't know how as I am not an electronics guru) that the laser was emitting.  Same thing happened over by Grand Forks Air Force Base this past Nov.. I knew there was a cop sittin in the area as my detector (the laser alert) would go off and he was over 6 miles away when he got somebody else and pulled me over  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Therefore, even if they do go off though, they will not work if you just happen to be the last vehicle in a group of cars and the fricken HP/Cop can't get his sorry @$$ out to catch the one he actually nailed.  You get the ticket regardless instead and end up payin somebody elses bill.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>YES! I have issues!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||TheFiero64||05-09-2001||12:28 PM||||Happy Belated B-day Steve, You were lucky not to get a ticket. <P>I got pulled over yesterday, I was not in the Fiero. I was picking up someone for work at 2:30 AM(early shift sucks) and was waiting at a red light. I saw the cop pull down a side street and turn around and park on the side of the street. I waited ten Min for the light to change and it was still red. I had my blinker on, looked both ways and went. He pulled me over right away. He got up to the car all cocky and said You just went through a red light. I explained that I watched him pull up and turn around, waited ten minutes and finally went because it must be a sensor light and is not going to change. He asked for my license and registration and left for his car yelling <B>"YOU ALSO HAVE A FREAKING HEADLIGHT OUT"</B>. He finally came back after I was late to pick up the worker and asked why I was 50 miles from my home address and in <B>"His Town!"</B> I explained that I work for UPS in the next town over and was sent to pick up a worker and don't know the area well. He said <B>"A $100 fine is not a good way to start the day"</B> WHAT? I went nuts. I said "you must be some kind of assh%$e." He YELLED <B>"LET ME FINNISH TALKING, I AM LETTING YOU OFF WITH A WARNING, if you ever go through a red light in my town again you will have more that a $100 fine to worry about.</B><P>I can't believe he was such an assh%$e. I should report him!<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fiero5||05-09-2001||12:41 PM||||If he let you off with a warning, I would just let it go this time.<BR>Steve||||reg||4
Z||000013||fiero56||05-09-2001||01:23 PM||||I almost got nailed yesterday. There were two lanes going my direction, and a damn 3000GT pulls out right in front of me. I Cut over to the open lane and decide to drop the hammer and pop right out in front of the Mitsu before my new lane ends in 1/8 mile. As I'm downshifting and putting my right foot to the floor, I notice a cop waiting to pull out off of a side street. I only had the chance to hit 50 in a 45, but he was on my a$$ <B>fast</B>running my plates, hoping to get me for something. I just cruised at 50mph figuring if I'm busted for 5 over, why slow down. He followed for a couple of miles, then turned around. If I hadn't seen him for another 50 yards, I would have been busted for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000014||mblackwell||05-09-2001||01:51 PM||||Cops will usually allow 5 mph over the limit to allow for speedometor calibration problems.  Some cops will allow 10 over because they don't like bothering with traffic offenders.  That probably doesn't apply to the state patrol though.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Ken Wittlief||05-09-2001||01:59 PM||||If the cops really wanted to bust some of us that would be the way to do it, get a nephew or someone in a riceburner and have them edge us on<P> right past their waiting laser trap!<P>Its always at the least expected times that they show up. I was driving across the state last week, pushing it a little 75 to 80 on and off on the thruway (65). When I was almost home I got boxed in on the right lane behind a truck, and everyone was slowing down for no apparent reason.<P>  I finally got out from behind the truck, into the fast lane, and was just about to wind it back up to 80 to get away from all the cars and<BR> <BR> oh, thats why everyone was slowing down to 60. there were about 4 state troopers set up in a big weekender speed trap.<P>  If I had seen them about 1 second later I would of had it floored.<P>  Speeding was a much bigger game back when the state highways were all at 55: fuzzbusters, CB radios, headlight flashers, letting someone run rabbit for you about 1/2 mile ahead and watching their brakelites for that 'OakWrap' reflex slam onthe brakes.<P>  But since most of the highways have opened up to 65 again, you can pretty much get away with 75 most of the time, which aint too bad.<P>  The thing that irks me the most is that our grandparents were driving 65 or more on the highways that Ike built back in the late 40s and 50s, and we are still driving 65 now - fifty years later!!!<P>   where is the leap in automotive technology that everything else got? We should be cruising the interstates at 120 - 180 mph by now, safely, quietly and economically.<P>   Except for the electonic fuel injection and ignition systems, cars really havent changed like everything else has in the last 50 years. We are way overdue!||||reg||1
Z||000016||Spektyr||05-09-2001||02:47 PM||||I used to have a mild Nissan pickup street racer.  I kept it looking stock so I could bait the local yokels into racing light to light for 20-40 bucks.  (Kept me in gas money quite nicely).  This was back when I was in the Navy in Florida.<P>Well, I got stationed in Mayport Fl, about 3 hrs from my girlfriend in Orlando, and drove there and back every weekend to see her.  One time on my way back to Mayport I got stuck in some nasty traffic for over an hour tooling along at 55mph in a 65.  Finally I worked my way through it, got the clean air in front of me and let her rip.  I had the speedo pegged at about 90 for a few seconds with it still accelerating, cruising up a hill when I started gaining on a semi-truck pretty quickly.  I take my foot off the gas, give it some brakes just as a Hi-po crests the hill with all his lights on.  He immediately busts a U-turn and gets up to speed about half a mile back from me.<P>Well, I figure I'm nailed, so I pass the truck with what's left of my speed, and start cruising in the right lane at 65mph, waiting for him to catch up and write me a gigantic ticket.  Watching my mirror, I can't see his lights anymore, and then just when I'm wondering what happened to me he comes flying by me at no less than 80mph.<P>I'm not entirely sure if he was after me, but my best guess is that he had clocked me when I'd been flying, but didn't think that my innocent-looking little truck had been the one he'd spotted earlier at well over 100mph.<P>Since then I've had very limited seat time at over 100, those tickets are <I>nasty</I>.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000017||Ken Wittlief||05-09-2001||03:05 PM||||yeah, I figure, if you really wanna go that fast take flying lessons or something. For the money it costs to get your hands on a serious 120+ mph car, you can buy a small plane that will go 180||||reg||1
Z||000018||JSocha||05-09-2001||04:43 PM||||I think police, when behind there badge, have gained way to much power.  And the judges haven't helped either as they have helped enforce this by backing them 200%.<P>Police/HP will initiate violations as well and who of us can really fight it in a court of law, as the judge will not want to loose either his golfing buddy or just because they work closely together.<P>In the winter of 1991, I went up to my GF town (Upham) to join her at the bar where a live band was playing that weekend (big deal around these parts to actually have a live band playin at a bar).<P>Yes, another long story from my personal diary of experiences or should I say, memoirs...memwaws (spelling? you get the picture).<P>After I left, in my '88 Chrysler Lebaron 4 whapper (w/o Turbo), I turned off onto the highway and where an HP cruiser was sitting on an approach about 50' away from the road I just turned off of.<P>Passed their position, no big deal (had to roll down my windows as they were tinted and I didn't want to get picked up for that).<P>Cruisin home at 60MPH (55MPH zone) minding my own business when headlights started getting closer and closer in my rear view mirror and radar detector never once going off.  Then the highbeams come on and the vehicle is now following right behind me to where I can just make out the grill (at 1AM in the morning yet).  He was so close and at the same time we are both in an area where it is heavy with deer crossing the highway at night as this area is bad.  If I would have even put my brakes on slightly, he would have plowed into me.  This went on for a couple of miles.  I then slowed down and pulled over slightly to the shoulder of the road and he stayed right there and didn't pass, headlights still on full and only a few feet from my rear bumper.  Then I sped back up to 60, him right behind me still.  Now I thought it was somebody from the bar that either knew me or wanted to make trouble.  I sped up to 105MPH and after a short while, vehicle was right behind me again.  Now if anything happened where I had to slam on my brakes to avoid a deer crossing, he would have went right over me or there would have been one hell of an accident.  I then slowed down to 90MPH and stayed at this speed for about a minute or two; car still behind me riding my @ss.  Almost to a town called Bantry.  Then I put my brake lights on, got down to 80MPH, then 40MPH, then 20MPH and then I pulled over to the side of the road to see who the heck was behind me.  The moment I stopped on the shoulder with the vehicle behind me doing the same, the moment I shifted my car into park, the "cherry's" went on.<P>Here it was the HP that was sitting on the approach.<P>I asked him what the "hell" he thinks he was doing following that close behind me, with his brights on in an area where deer could come out at any moment.<P>He tells me he clocked me doing 65MPH when I passed him where he was sitting and followed me.  Besides this being a bunch of BS, cause no car that I know can get from 0-65 MPH in less then 50', which I told him.  I told him had I had to have put on my brakes for any reason, we would both probably be dead.  He just shrugged his shoulders.  Then he tells me he is giving me a ticket for doing 88MPH in a 55MPH zone, when he was following me at 105MPH!<P>I told him I was going to contest it.  He tells me "go right ahead, it will be your word against mine and I will always win".<P>Talked to a lawyer, was going to go on my own as the lawyer even said there would be nothing I could do as I don't have any witnesses.<P>So I don't contest it even though I want to.<P>Then, later that summer, I find out that the same Towner HP who did this to me from Upham, did this with a teenage girl coming home from a B-Ball game late one night where he actually touched bumpers with her and scared her so much that she tried to outrun him.  She lost the court case.<P>A guy who owns the lumber yard here in town had the same thing happen to him where the same HP followed him and his wife closely on HWY 2 near Towner, got him to pickup speed and then ticketed him once he got him over 80MPH in a 55MPH zone.<P>Back in 1999, he was finally caught doing this.  Some kids going down the same Upham road I had been ticketed coming back on were coming back from a Bottineau Football game and had 3 video cameras with them and unbenounced to him had filmed him from start to finish with his actions.  One camera had filmed the speed of their vehicle, while the other two were filming the HP and actually hitting their vehicle and anytime they slowed down, he would nudge them again and get them to speed, even when they tried to pull over.  They even had him on film coming up to the door and saying the reason why he pulled them over was for doing so many MPH in a 55MPH zone.  The kid I guess was actually bold enough to say he was going to contest it where the HP also told them "it would be there word against his".<P>The kids (and the father of one of the other kids) was in court and after the judge ruled in favor for the cop, the father pulled out a tape and said "Would you like to see what really happened" to the judge.  The States Attorney wasn't interested (but wondering why it wasn't shown) however the Judge didn't care what was on the tape.  The father from what I recall reading, gave the judge an ultimatum, that either he watches what is on the tape and what really happened that evening, or he would have not one, but both their jobs vacant.  Judge said his ruling was final and that was it.<P>Subsequently, the Towner HP was fired never to work in law enforcement again and the judge was requested to step down after a hearing was performed because it was later learned that the HP and judge were somehow in cohootz with each other and this little "touch bumper" scam.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||Fiero5||05-10-2001||10:23 AM||||Well, the Formula got her inspection sticker this morning. However....<BR>Now a weird problem. We replaced both front parking light sockets and they work fine now, but now the headlights don't seem to have enough power to lift the doors up anymore. They worked just fine hours before we put in the replacement sockets. Would a bad ground or something similar on one of the new sockets be drawing just enough power away so the headlights don't have that extra power to push up the headlight doors?<BR>What's up with that?<P>Steve<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroSSsignature1_1.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000020||FieroJoe||05-10-2001||10:56 AM||||Check to make sure that you dont have a short to ground from the wiring you did when you replaced the sockets.  Also, just double check the connections at the motors, you could have jiggled something around when you replaced the sockets!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
